<title>FINLAND: EX-PM AHO SAYS NO TO EMU WITH CURRENT GOVT POLICY.</title>
<headline>EX-PM AHO SAYS NO TO EMU WITH CURRENT GOVT POLICY.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Opposition leader and Centre Party chairman Esko Aho said on Tuesday that Finnish membership of EMU was not compatible with the current high unemployment and the widening of regional differences.</p>
<p>&quot;The current level of unemployment and wider regional differences coupled with EMU-membership create an impossible equation,&quot; Aho told parliamenmt during a plenary debate initiated by an interpellation submitted by his party against the ruling left-right-green coalition.</p>
<p>&quot;The key question is whether it makes sense for Finland to join the single currency among the first,&quot; Aho said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
